  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 in full plus the AI Search index catalog doc.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Index definitions as content">Move the 7 canonical index JSON bodies (currently inline in the script's REST payloads) into embedded resource/content files consumed by the new provisioner.</step>
    <step order="2" name="SearchIndexClientProvisioner">Author the collaborator using SearchIndexClient under UAMI RBAC (Azure.Search.Documents.Indexes), create-or-update each of the 7 indexes, no admin-key anywhere.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Real tenant-filter provisioner">Author AiSearchTenantFilterTemplateProvisioner performing the ACTUAL template provisioning (not a log+Success stub) -- provision the tenant-scoped filter template artifact the existing real verifier checks against.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Wire up">Replace DeployAllIndexesScriptProvisioner and StubAiSearchTenantFilterTemplateProvisioner in H2b's owning module with the two new real implementations.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Tests">7-index create/verify tests + template idempotency tests (re-run produces no-op) per DS-4 §7's test-effort note.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green; grep 'admin-key\|adminKey' in the new provisioner returns 0 matches.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If provisioning the real tenant-filter template requires a template SCHEMA the existing (already-real) verifier does not document anywhere in code (i.e., the verifier checks for an artifact shape this task must reverse-engineer), STOP and read the verifier's assertion logic FIRST as the authoritative schema source before authoring the provisioner — do not invent a template shape independently of what the verifier actually checks.</trigger>
