  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 is the canonical 7-index catalog authority (this project's own CLAUDE.md names it so); the real verifier already exists. Extension -- porting the provisioner side to SDK while KEEPING the verifier unchanged is the correct minimal extension. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H2b cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site; separately, the I2 tenant-isolation invariant's RUNTIME-provisioning half stays permanently unenforced (only the ArchTest's static-scan half exists today), meaning a live AI Search tenant-filter template could silently be absent even though the code that WOULD check for it exists.

COMPLETION SUMMARY (2026-08-19, commit ad36052f0): SearchIndexClientProvisioner replaces DeployAllIndexesScriptProvisioner -- constructs Azure.Search.Documents.Indexes.SearchIndexClient per-request bound to the customer's search endpoint, using the shared UAMI-pinned TokenCredential singleton (registered by CosmosModule); zero admin-key handling anywhere (verified by test + code inspection). Because Azure.Search.Documents 11.6.0's SearchIndex model has no public JSON-read path (IUtf8JsonSerializable is write-only in this SDK version), the 7 canonical index JSON bodies are embedded verbatim (checksum-verified) from infrastructure/ai-search/*.json as .csproj EmbeddedResource entries and PUT via SearchIndexClient.Pipeline (the SDK's own documented low-level extensibility seam) rather than hand-retyped into C# object graphs -- this keeps ONE source of truth for the schema catalog. AiSearchTenantFilterTemplateProvisioner replaces StubAiSearchTenantFilterTemplateProvisioner with a real Cosmos-backed implementation: new ITenantFilterTemplateStore seam + CosmosTenantFilterTemplateStore writing to a NEW, TTL-less `tenantFilterTemplates` container (deliberately separate from the 365-day-TTL `runs` container -- a tenant-isolation control must outlive any single ProvisioningRun's retention window) on the SAME shared Cosmos account/client L2 already owns. Idempotency is a genuine content-comparison no-op (re-running with unchanged inputs performs zero writes), not merely PUT-safe overwrite. H2bAiSearchIndexHandler.cs required NO logic changes -- proof the wave-C4 seam design was correct; only DI bindings + stale doc-comments referencing the retired script were updated. Escalation trigger did NOT fire: no pre-existing verifier of the template ARTIFACT's schema was found in code (RestApiAiSearchIndexVerifier verifies per-index tenantId-filterable-field presence, a different invariant); the artifact shape was designed fresh from the interface's own documented seam contract, with task 173 (I2 acceptance probe) explicitly deferring to a live sample-query check rather than re-reading this artifact. 20 new tests (13 SearchIndexClientProvisionerTests incl. real-SDK fake-transport tests mirroring task 121's ArmSdkTestFakes pattern; 7 AiSearchTenantFilterTemplateProvisionerTests incl. explicit idempotency + tenant-change-triggers-overwrite proofs). Verified in isolation on top of commit 17f74cd46: 851/851 passing, 0 build warnings/errors. Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Program.cs and Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core.csproj are shared composition-root files also being edited concurrently by sibling task 123 (H2a); this task's commit contains ONLY the H2b-scoped hunks (verified via a clean-checkout isolated rebuild+test), leaving task 123's BicepInfraDeploy/*.cs changes uncommitted in the working tree for that task to commit separately.</notes>

